Z||000000||mwbackus||02-06-2000||12:56 PM||||The Fiero Store has a new / improved web site now!  You can even order online.  They also have a downloadable price list(PDF).  This provides for searching of a price without being online.  Something I find valuble since my price lists are always chopped up, (eg.. the order form is on the back of the thing).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <P>PS.  Please disregard this FYI if, like many here, you use the FS site as your start-up page. You would undoubtable already know this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-06-2000||01:38 PM||||I grant that Fiero Store has allot of nice things, even some hard to get ones, but always remember to shop wrenchead.com and your local stores first for engine/tranny/chassis parts. And if the local store says it's a dealer only part then check wrenchead.com they have allot of AC-delco and other parts the local chain stores don't have. There are a couple other online parts stores that also have "dealer only" parts. The prices are nearly always less than Fiero Store.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-06-2000||06:17 PM||||Good point, ogre, but let me add something.  Assuming you don't need the part yesterday, you might try asking to see if anyone here has what you're looking for.  You'd be surprised at the # of things we have that we can't use anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||02-06-2000||09:03 PM||||I just bought both l/r dew strips from the Fiero Store to prevent my new glass from scratching and they costed me $82.00 with shipping! They showed up in a GM box and I'm wondering if I would've saved a few bucks ordering straight from them instead?||||reg||2
Z||000004||2FAST4U||02-06-2000||09:17 PM||||I'll admit that the Fiero Store does cost a little more sometimes. Sometimes paying a little extra is worth it. The last time I ordered something from the GM dealer for my Fireo it took about a month to get the stuss. when I order from the Fiero Store I can usually expect it to be on my door step in three or four days. To me the friendly staff and quick service are worth a few extra bucks.<P>I guess thats my 2 cents worth<P>2FAST4U||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||02-06-2000||09:18 PM||||Ok, remember this, if you don’t support the Fiero Store type companies, they will go out of business.  And then there goes some of those niche type items just for Fieros. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||02-07-2000||12:20 AM||||The other thing about the Fiero Store is they made "lifetime" purchases from GM. So even though the part at the Fiero store is a "Genuine GM" part, the parts may not be available at the dealerships anymore. While restoring my '86 there were quite a few parts no longer available at the dealer but the ones ordered from FS were GM parts. ||||reg||1
