Z||000013||mwbackus||02-07-2000||11:20 PM||||MM:<BR>The active desktop is a feature of Windows 98 that allows you to use an actual web page as your background image.  You can update it on demand, or schedule it for timed updates.  Actually, it eats up alot of resources, and I do not recommend using it unless your system is sufficiently powered.<P><BR>Mike||||reg||1
