Z||000015||superXmotorsports||02-08-2000||06:35 PM||||Any more I buy something from the Fiero Store once a week.  I've always had good service with them.  There have been a couple things that were lower elsewhere but you just have to shop around.  The local Pontiac dealer assured me that $70 was giving me a deal on an ignition module so in a pinch I said OK.  Fiero Store price - $30!  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000016||william_thorniii||02-08-2000||07:41 PM||||Gokart,<P>Again I know that this has been covered in the past but here goes:<P>Chriswell Chevrolet 503 Quince Orchard Rd. Gaithersburg, Md. 20878 <BR>Dealer phone 301-948-0880 <BR>Parts Dept. 888-466-9101 <BR>Parts Dept. Fax 301-670-0936 <BR>Parts Dept. direct 301-590-1458 <BR>Since this is a large operation, Chris asks that you first talk to Kevin <BR>Burdette in the parts dept. and identify yourself as a Fiero list member <BR>to get the "trade" price on any GM parts. If he is busy, or if you have <BR>any questions, <BR>you can ask for Chris. Parts prices will be the same he was able to offer <BR>through Galaxy, and yes, they will UPS at no charge for shipping, BUT, <BR>this dealership will charge all purchasers (any state) a 5% Maryland tax. <BR>Apparently <BR>there are enforceable intrastate mail order tax laws that Chriswell feels <BR>they must abide by to avoid any tax collection problems. To new list <BR>members, you can order any GM part at a discount that usually runs 20-30% <BR>off retail list. Chris has been excellent to work with in the past, and <BR>certainly can save you substantial $$$ on your Fiero parts needs. <BR>Galaxy Pontiac where Chris used to be at still is offering the same <BR>discounts. Plus no tax. Give them a try. 1-800-225-1113.<P>This is an excerpt from an original post from "Dogtired" or Dave Bonner.  I have not checked my credit card statement to be able to verify what happened with the tax/shipping charges as of yet.  Regardless of the amount, I have been EXTREMELY satisfied with my service.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000017||DXR_DAD||02-08-2000||08:34 PM||||This goes with another post (Buying Parts)<P>Do all of you/us look for the best deal on parts? and is if any different when buying used parts. There are lots of mail order parts houses the offer free shippping. I have  bought parts from fourm members and the total price w/shipping was less than what I could have got the part here (Calif.) This is fourm is one of the ways I look for the best deal?<P>Fiero Shop this also why some people say that some places are to high, every thing here in Cali is big bucks$$$$$$. Still paying $1.87 at the pump!!||||reg||1
